Root cause:
The bug was caused by a missing bounds check for the variable "idx" in the function `amdgpu_set_pp_force_state()`. The code did not ensure that "idx" was less than the size of the `data.states` array (which has a size of 16). This could lead to out-of-bounds access when accessing `data.states[idx]`, potentially causing undefined behavior or crashes. The patch added a check to ensure that "idx" is within valid bounds after converting it from the input string. Additionally, the variable "idx" was changed to an unsigned type to prevent negative values from being processed.
